What you must deliver
•	A runnable Spring Boot repository with documented setup and no committed secrets.
•	A fraud case intake API and participant-friendly UI.
•	A framework-neutral FraudCaseProcessor contract with rules mode plus a Spring AI or LangChain4j implementation; implementing both is a comparison extension.
•	At least four distinct evidence tools, deterministic synthetic fixtures and an observable execution trace.
•	Policy ingestion, vector retrieval, exact citation metadata and abstention when policy context is insufficient.
•	Case-scoped conversation memory, persistence for cases/evidence/recommendations/reviews, and an append-only audit trail.
•	Schema-validated recommendation output and a human-review screen that records the final disposition and rationale.
•	Unit, integration, contract and evaluation tests; a README, architecture view, screenshots and self-review.
Explicitly out of scope
•	Production customer data, payment credentials, unmasked identifiers or real bank connectivity.
•	Autonomous financial, account-control, compliance or customer-contact actions.
•	Unbounded tool permissions, silent policy changes or model output that bypasses application validation.
•	Hidden chain-of-thought display. Show concise reasons, evidence, tool outcomes and policy passages instead.
1. Capstone brief
1.1 Business problem
Payment-dispute teams receive cases with incomplete narratives and evidence distributed across transaction, customer, device, merchant, earlier-dispute and policy systems. Analysts must identify the dispute type, determine urgency, locate the applicable procedure and record why a case was routed to a particular queue. The capstone assistant accelerates those tasks while preserving human control.
1.2 Primary users and value
User	Need	Capstone response
Service agent	Capture a complete case without exposing sensitive data.	Guided intake, validation, masking and a visible missing-information list.
Fraud investigator	Collect and compare relevant signals quickly.	Tool-driven enrichment, evidence severity and a chronological trace.
Dispute reviewer	Apply the correct process and queue.	Policy-grounded recommendation with citations and human-review controls.
Team lead / auditor	Reproduce what happened.	Saved facts, tool results, retrieved passages, recommendation, disposition and audit events.

1.3 Sample scenario
SCENARIO	A customer reports an online purchase from a merchant they do not recognise. The payment was made from a newly observed device and a location inconsistent with recent trusted activity. The customer still has the card. The transaction is posted, but the authentication outcome is unavailable. The analyst must distinguish unauthorised use, merchant/billing dispute, duplicate processing or insufficient evidence.

1.4 Success criteria
•	A reviewer can create the sample case and see validated, masked intake data.
•	The application selects approved tools, records arguments and outcomes, and never invents unavailable evidence.
•	Relevant policy passages are retrieved with document ID, version, section, chunk ID and score.
•	The recommendation conforms to the agreed schema, cites evidence and policy, lists missing information and always requires human review.
•	The reviewer can accept, revise, reroute or reject the recommendation with a mandatory reason; the action is audited.
•	Rules mode remains usable when the model is disabled; errors fail safely to incomplete/manual review.
2. Functional design
2.1 End-to-end journey
Step	Stage	Required behaviour
1	Intake	Validate mandatory fields; mask customer and payment identifiers.
2	Plan	Classify the investigation goal and create a bounded evidence plan.
3	Act	Invoke allow-listed transaction, device, location, merchant, history and SLA tools.
4	Retrieve	Search approved policy content; retain passage metadata and similarity scores.
5	Assess	Compare user facts, tool evidence and policy; identify contradictions and gaps.
6	Recommend	Return a typed classification, risk, route, rationale, evidence and citations.
7	Review	Require a human disposition and rationale before closing or routing the case.
8	Audit	Persist important state changes, tool traces, citations and review actions.

2.2 Case states
State	Meaning	Allowed next state
NEW	Case captured but not enriched.	ENRICHING
ENRICHING	Tools and policy retrieval are running.	READY_FOR_REVIEW or INCOMPLETE
INCOMPLETE	Required evidence is missing, contradictory or unavailable.	ENRICHING or CLOSED
READY_FOR_REVIEW	Validated recommendation is available.	UNDER_REVIEW
UNDER_REVIEW	A reviewer is evaluating the recommendation.	ROUTED or CLOSED
ROUTED	Reviewer selected an operational route.	CLOSED
CLOSED	Final disposition and audit data are recorded.	No transition

