3. Decision model and output contract
3.1 Classification and route
Classification	Typical evidence	Recommended route
UNAUTHORISED_TRANSACTION	Customer denies merchant; independent device/location/authentication anomalies.	FRAUD_INVESTIGATION
MERCHANT_DISPUTE	Customer recognises merchant but disputes fulfilment, cancellation or amount.	DISPUTE_OPERATIONS
DUPLICATE_PROCESSING	Matching payment fingerprint or duplicate posting evidence.	PAYMENT_OPERATIONS
SUSPICIOUS_TRANSACTION	High-risk signals exist but the customer claim does not establish unauthorised use.	FRAUD_INVESTIGATION
INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE	Required evidence unavailable, contradictory or below retrieval threshold.	MANUAL_REVIEW
GENUINE_TRANSACTION	Evidence supports customer-authorised activity; still subject to reviewer confirmation.	MANUAL_REVIEW

3.2 Deterministic fallback rules
•	If mandatory evidence is missing, return INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE and require manual review.
•	If a duplicate transaction fingerprint is confirmed, recommend PAYMENT_OPERATIONS.
•	If multiple independently sourced high-severity anomalies are present, recommend FRAUD_INVESTIGATION.
•	If the merchant is recognised and the issue concerns fulfilment, cancellation or amount, recommend DISPUTE_OPERATIONS.
•	If no policy passage meets the configured threshold, do not invent a procedure; identify the gap and route to manual review.
•	Every deterministic result must include rule IDs and the exact input facts used.
