3.4 Validation rules
•	Parse model output into a typed DTO and validate it before persistence or display.
•	Reject unknown enum values, confidence outside 0–1, missing case ID or malformed citations.
•	Require at least one evidence item or an explicit insufficient-evidence outcome.
•	Require humanReviewRequired=true for every recommendation.
•	Require citation metadata when the rationale claims a procedural requirement.
•	Do not expose hidden reasoning. Store and display only concise rationale, evidence links, citations and operational trace.
4. Solution architecture
4.1 Architecture principles
•	Keep domain entities, rules, persistence and controllers independent of the Java AI framework.
•	Separate deterministic evidence collection from model-assisted interpretation.
•	Keep state transitions in application services, not in model output.
•	Wrap provider/model/vector-store details in adapters selected through configuration.
•	Persist provenance: every important fact should identify user intake, tool result, policy retrieval or reviewer entry.
4.2 Logical layers
Layer	Key components	Responsibility
Experience	REST API, Thymeleaf UI	Case intake, investigation workspace, evidence, citations and review.
Application	FraudCaseService, InvestigationOrchestrator	Validate, authorise, transition state, invoke processor and persist results.
Domain	FraudCase, EvidenceItem, Recommendation, ReviewDisposition	Framework-neutral business contract, enums and invariants.
AI adapters	SpringAiFraudCaseAgent, LangChain4jFraudCaseAgent	Prompts, tool registration, memory, retrieval augmentation and typed output.
Rules adapter	RulesFraudCaseAgent	Deterministic fallback with rule IDs and no model dependency.
Tools	EvidenceTools and approved adapters	Structured, deterministic evidence with provenance and safe failure.
Knowledge	PolicyIngestionService, PolicyRetriever	Chunk, embed, search, threshold, cite and abstain.
Persistence	JPA repositories and audit writer	Cases, evidence, traces, citations, recommendations and review actions.
Observability	Metrics, traces and redacted logs	Correlation ID, latency, status and errors without sensitive payloads.

