10. Responsible AI, security and operations
Risk	Required control	Evidence to show
Sensitive data leakage	Synthetic/masked data; field allow-list; output/log redaction; retention limits.	Fixtures, masking tests and redacted logs.
Hallucinated evidence	Typed tools; provenance; schema validation; abstention.	Missing-evidence and malformed-output tests.
Unsupported policy claim	Thresholded RAG; exact citation metadata; passage display.	No-match test and citation screen.
Prompt injection	Treat case text and policy passages as untrusted data; preserve system/tool boundaries.	Injection tests and recorded result.
Excessive permissions	Read-only allow-listed tools; least-privilege filesystem/repository/MCP scope; timeouts.	Tool registry and scoped configuration.
Autonomous action	No card block, refund, credit, transfer, report or contact tool.	Guardrail test; humanReviewRequired always true.
Cross-case leakage	Case-keyed memory and authorisation on every case endpoint.	Isolation and access-control tests.
Audit tampering	Append-only events; reviewer identity; payload hash; restricted update/delete.	Repository test and audit view.
Model/provider outage	Rules path and manual-review safe state.	Failure test with model disabled.
Unfair or opaque routing	Evidence-linked rationale; no protected-attribute use; reviewer control.	Feature allow-list and review checklist.

NEVER AUTOMATE	The capstone may recommend a route, priority or evidence request. It must not execute a financial, customer-impacting, compliance or account-control action.

10.1 Observability requirements
•	Generate a correlation ID for every investigation and propagate it across application, tool, retrieval and model spans.
•	Record tool name, status, duration and redacted result summary; record retrieval count/scores and model latency.
•	Do not log raw prompts or responses by default when they may contain case data; use hashes and approved summaries.
•	Expose health for database, configured model provider and vector store without revealing credentials.
•	Alert or visibly flag repeated tool failures, invalid-output rate and unavailable policy retrieval.
